#
# psk.txt - Pre-Shared Key File Format (racoon.conf.5, "Pre-shared key File")
#
# Referenced from racoon.conf via:
#   path pre_shared_key "/etc/racoon/psk.txt";
#
# and consulted whenever a "remote" block's proposal uses one of the
# pre_shared_key/xauth_psk_server/xauth_psk_client/hybrid_rsa_*
# authentication methods.
#
# This file must be owned by the user racoon runs as (normally root) and
# must not be readable by anyone else:
#   chmod 600 /etc/racoon/psk.txt
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Syntax
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One entry per line: an identifier, then whitespace, then the secret key.
# The identifier's format must match the peer's my_identifier/xauth_login
# type -- an address, an FQDN, a USER_FQDN (user@domain), or an ASN.1 DN --
# whichever the peer actually sends during phase 1 (or, for XAuth, whatever
# xauth_login names).  Everything after the first run of whitespace is the
# key, so the key itself may contain spaces.
#
# Lines starting with "#" are comments.  A key starting with "0x" is
# interpreted as a hexadecimal string rather than literal text.
#
# Use long, high-entropy keys (>= 20 random characters).  A short or
# guessable PSK is the weakest link in any pre-shared-key deployment,
# and pre-shared-key + Aggressive Mode is especially exposed to offline
# dictionary attacks -- see racoon-admin-guide.html §8.3 "Aggressive Mode
# Considerations".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Examples (replace with your own identifiers and generated keys --
# e.g. `openssl rand -base64 24` for a fresh random key)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Address identifier (my_identifier/peers_identifier address):
# 192.0.2.10          Kj8x2mQpR9vLNz4wTgY6uH3sD7fB1eAc

# FQDN identifier (my_identifier fqdn "gw.example.com"):
# gw.example.com      Kj8x2mQpR9vLNz4wTgY6uH3sD7fB1eAc

# USER_FQDN identifier (my_identifier user_fqdn "alice@example.com"),
# also the form used for xauth_login "alice":
# alice@example.com   Kj8x2mQpR9vLNz4wTgY6uH3sD7fB1eAc

# Hexadecimal key:
# 198.51.100.4        0x4b6a3878326d5170523976

# XAuth password for xauth_login "alice" (see
# examples/roadwarrior/client/racoon.conf's xauth_login directive) --
# for xauth_rsa_client the identifier is the login name, not a peer
# address, since the RSA signature (not the PSK) does the phase 1
# authentication and this entry only supplies the XAuth password:
# alice                correct-horse-battery-staple
